            // Data: semi-structured and unstructured
            B.q("sa-m4-22", "sa-nonrelational", "Millions of devices write a reading every minute to Cosmos DB, and most queries ask for one device's readings. Which partition key avoids hot partitions and keeps queries cheap?", listOf("The reading's date", "The device ID", "A constant such as 'readings'", "The reading's sensor type"), setOf(1), "A good partition key has many distinct values that spread writes evenly, and matches the most common query filter. Device ID does both: writes spread over millions of keys, and a device's readings sit in one partition.",
                scenario = "Hedgehog Home's Android app shows each household its smart-meter readings. Two million meters write to Cosmos DB every minute.",
